# fence-pylon - Area 3 laser-fence pylon (orbital emitter node; the developer draws the wall). 16x16, 2 frames,
# straight top-down, left-right symmetric shape. light: top-left. K exterior outline, seams where jaws meet hull.
# Layout: steel octagonal hull (cols 4-11, rows 1-14); one emitter jaw each side (cols 0-3 and 12-15, rows 4-11):
# steel prongs on rows 5 and 10 around an open mouth (cols 0-1 / 14-15, rows 7-8) with a 2x2 red lens
# (cols 2-3 left, 12-13 right, rows 7-8).
# Wall attach: frame side edges, centre y=8 (edge coords, between rows 7 and 8), as pylon.px. A wall drawn from
# lx+6 to rx-6 (render/world.ts) runs through the open mouths and meets the lenses at edge x=14 / x=2.
# Use the same sprite for both pylons, unmirrored (mirroring would flip the top-left light).
# Palette: steel 1 2 3 4 5, red n r p, fire-4 W, K (10 colours). Lens matches the fence wall ramp.
# Frames: 0 idle (lens r over n), 1 pulse (lens W/p, hot like the wall's hot line). 200 ms each, loop.
# Option for the developer: show idle while the wall is off and pulse during flicker/on. Anchor: frame centre (8,8).
palette
. transparent
K #0b0d1a  outline
1 #1c2238  steel-0
2 #2f3a5a  steel-1
3 #4a5a82  steel-2
4 #7184ad  steel-3
5 #a7b8d8  steel-4
n #92203a  red-1
r #da3d4f  red-2
p #ff8a86  red-3
W #fff0b8  fire-4 glint
ramp steel 1 2 3 4 5
ramp red n r p
frame idle 200
